# hub.json, leaderboard.json, challenges.json and tacmap.json used to be
# ignored here, on the reasoning that they hold coordinates which only mean
# something in the world they were set in, so committing them would aim the
# droplet's boards at wherever the local test world's happened to be.
#
# That reasoning inverted the moment data/world/ became tracked and the
# droplet started running THIS world. The coordinates now mean exactly the
# same thing on both machines, and ignoring them shipped a world full of
# hologram entities with nothing to drive them: the droplet had no board
# positions, so every board froze displaying text baked into the world file
# at its last local refresh, and hub.json being absent meant the hub spawn
# teleport silently never ran there at all.
#
# They are coordinates only - no UUIDs, no player names - so they are safe
# in a public repo. Checked before untracking; keep it that way.
data/kubejs/config/live_board.json
data/kubejs/config/micromap.json
# starter_chests.json stays ignored for a different reason that has NOT
# inverted: it records which player claimed which chest, by UUID and name.
# That is per-player data and does not belong in a public repo.
data/kubejs/config/starter_chests.json
